    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `capacityWarning` field so it returns `true` when the owner's city already holds 40\u201349 other owners (approaching the hard limit of 50); the existing 50-owner rejection is untouched.\n\nChanges, kept structurally minimal by mirroring the existing warning idiom:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `capacityWarning` boolean property to the `Owner` schema (next to `bulkSignupWarning`), which regenerates `OwnerDto` with the getter/setter.\n2. **`CapacityWarning.java`** (new) \u2014 a small, self-contained static helper `of(Owner, OwnerRepository)` that counts other owners in the same city (case-insensitive, trimmed, self excluded by id) and returns `true` for a count in `[40, 49]`, exactly mirroring `BulkSignupWarning`. It short-circuits and returns `false` once the count exceeds 49 (that's the hard-limit territory).\n3. **`RespondWithOwner.java`** \u2014 one added line, `dto.setCapacityWarning(CapacityWarning.of(owner, ownerRepository));`, alongside the existing warning wiring.\n\nWhy this keeps structural impact low: the new logic lives in its own cohesive class with zero surrounding complexity (WMC_other = 0), and the only edit to an existing function is a single line in a single-method class, so no method or class was grown. `RejectOwnerCityAtCapacity` and its escalation path are unchanged.\n\nFull suite: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**.",
